    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The ultimate goal was to advance, through evaluation of present knowledge and of the results of new coordinated research, the states of the art and the practice in the earthquake-resistant design of high-rise reinforced concrete (RC) buildings. To achieve this goal, particular emphasis was placed on:\r\n- identification of RC buildings systems which are particularly suitable for high-rise construction in seismic regions with soft-soil sites;\r\n- evaluation of seismic response characteristics of these systems, considering linear and nonlinear responses;\r\n- development of new computer programs for computer analysis of 3-D nonlinear responses;\r\n- evaluation of recent developments in energy dissipation mechanisms for possible integration into these systems;\r\n- use of high strength concrete (500 to 670 kg/cm2); and\r\n- development of improved methods of preliminaiy design to enhance seismic performance of these systems.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Inoue, Norio and Suzuki, Norio and Morikawa, Hiroshi and Okano, Masaaki and Fukuda, Takaharu and Hatamoto, Hitoshi and Takahashi, Motomi and Orui, Satoshi and Maruta, Makoto and Bertero, Vitelmo V and Krawinkler, Helmut and Anderson, James C and Powell, Graham H and Filippou, Filip C and Goucha, Hatem Y and Seneviratna, Pasan and Rahnama, Mohsen and Teran-Gilmore, Amador and Bertero, Raul D. (1993). Design of High-Rise Reinforced Concrete Building. CUREE-Kajima Research Project Report CKI-19. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/dq523tw9253",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
